Unix is a trade mark, and with proprietary copyrighted source codes. 
Linux was written to look-and-feel like a unix system with alternative original
codes. The short answer is, linux is not and cannot be called unix *legally*, 
but from a user's point of view, it works and functions like a unix system.   

