I think I once use DEC's own cc on DU 4.0d to build egcs 1.1.2 a while ago. 
You just need to do "make bootstrap" instead of make to use the native 
compiler to build gcc. It goes through a 3-stage bootstrap - take longer and 
use more space, but usually works on non-linux/non-gcc builts :-). Your current
gcc is probably a bit broken; use the native compiler and do a 3-stage bootstrap
instead.

